v8.29 — IARC content rating in the App Store's grammar + multi picker

Google Play and Epic share buildAndroidContentRatingSection, so both change.
It was 14 numbered cards with vertical radio/checkbox lists, follow-ups as
further cards, auto-collapsing into summary rows. Now it is drawn the way the
App Store / Mac questionnaire is:

- Seven theme bands (Violence and Fear, Sexuality, Language and Humor,
  Drugs/Alcohol/Tobacco, Gambling and Purchases, Online Features, Sensitive
  Content) instead of a 1-14 count; long top-level titles shortened, IARC's
  wording kept in the hint.
- One row per question: Yes/No as yn-btn, single-selects as intensity-btn
  pills. Answers always stay in the right-hand column; a long question
  wraps onto more lines instead of pushing its pills underneath.
- Multi-selects are a picker (swSelect's pill + dropdown with tick boxes):
  every row keeps the same one-line shape, so follow-ups line up under it in
  option order. Stays open while ticking (state.giarcPickerOpen), closes via
  closeAllDropdowns; violet when Shipmate's, grey "Select all that apply"
  when empty.
- Follow-ups on the .ios-followup rail under the row that reveals them. A
  multi-select option that opens several questions names the group
  ("Against humans") and the children drop the repeated prefix.
- Short pill labels for long IARC options (GIARC_SHORT_OPT), full text in
  the hint. Presentation only: answers stay IARC option indices.
- Violet = written by Shipmate (inference or App Store mapping); pressing a
  violet pill confirms it, pressing a blue one clears it (answerIOSField's
  rule). Meta is spread on confirm so provenance survives.
- Pinned Unanswered/All bar with "Shipmate answered X of 14". Snapshot is
  per top-level branch (state.giarcAnsweredAtSnapshot), taken after
  inference (egs now included in _postInferenceSetup) and the first time
  the App Store mapping fills anything.

(v8.28 was a local cache-bust only, never published.)

Removed: the card/collapse renderer, toggleGIARCExpand, the
giarcManuallyExpanded/Collapsed sets and the .giarc-card CSS.
